# PAN-OS Management Auth From Unexpected Source  (CVE-2026-0322)
# Source rule: ../sigma/pan_os_mgmt_auth_from_unexpected_source.yml
# Write-up:    https://www.sohankanna.com/research/cve-2026-0322-pan-os-management-interface-zero-day-from-admin-login-to-root
#
# Requires: Splunk Add-on for Palo Alto Networks (Splunk_TA_paloalto).
#   PAN-OS SYSTEM log forwarded as sourcetype pan:system (admin auth events).
#   Field names below follow the add-on's CIM mapping; adjust if you use raw syslog.
# NOTE: this detects UNEXPECTED management-plane auth - it is NOT proof that
#   CVE-2026-0322 was exploited. It uses cidrmatch() for real CIDR matching
#   (the generic `sigma convert -t splunk` renders |cidr as a literal string
#   equality, which is wrong - use this file, or a CIDR-aware Splunk pipeline).
# TUNE: src_allowlist = your jump-box / admin CIDRs.

sourcetype=pan:system subtype=auth (action=success OR event_desc="*authenticated*" OR result="success")
| where NOT (cidrmatch("10.0.0.0/8", src_ip))      ``` TUNE: add each approved admin CIDR as another cidrmatch() OR clause ```
| stats count min(_time) as firstTime max(_time) as lastTime by admin, src_ip, event_desc, vsys, host
| `security_content_ctime(firstTime)` | `security_content_ctime(lastTime)`
| sort - count
